    row
      text Expand description
      col
        text A support library for macro authors when defining new macros.
        text "This library, provided by the standard distribution, provides the types consumed in the interfaces of procedurally defined macro definitions such as function-like macros #[proc_macro], macro attributes #[proc_macro_attribute] and custom derive attributes #[proc_macro_derive]."
        text See  for more.
        link "the book" ../book/ch19-06-macros.html#procedural-macros-for-generating-code-from-attributes
    h2 Modules§
    row
      link token_stream token_stream/index.html
      text Public implementation details for the TokenStream type, such as iterators.
      row
        link tracked tracked/index.html
        text Experimental
      text Functionality for adding environment state to the build dependency info.
    h2 Macros§
    row
      row
        link quote macro.quote.html
        text Experimental
      text "quote!(..) accepts arbitrary tokens and expands into a TokenStream describing the input. For example, quote!(a + b) will produce an expression, that, when evaluated, constructs the TokenStream [Ident(\"a\"), Punct('+', Alone), Ident(\"b\")]."
    h2 Structs§
    row
      link Group struct.Group.html
      text A delimited token stream.
      link Ident struct.Ident.html
      text An identifier (ident).
      link LexError struct.LexError.html
      text "Error returned from TokenStream::from_str."
      link Literal struct.Literal.html
      text "A literal string (\"hello\"), byte string (b\"hello\"), C string (c\"hello\"), character ('a'), byte character (b'a'), an integer or floating point number with or without a suffix (1, 1u8, 2.3, 2.3f32). Boolean literals like true and false do not belong here, they are Idents."
      link Punct struct.Punct.html
      text "A Punct is a single punctuation character such as +, - or #."
      link Span struct.Span.html
      text A region of source code, along with macro expansion information.
      link TokenStream struct.TokenStream.html
      text The main type provided by this crate, representing an abstract stream of tokens, or, more specifically, a sequence of token trees. The type provides interfaces for iterating over those token trees and, conversely, collecting a number of token trees into one stream.
      row
        link Diagnostic struct.Diagnostic.html
        text Experimental
      text A structure representing a diagnostic message and associated children messages.
      row
        link ExpandError struct.ExpandError.html
        text Experimental
      text "Error returned from TokenStream::expand_expr."
    h2 Enums§
    row
      link Delimiter enum.Delimiter.html
      text Describes how a sequence of token trees is delimited.
      link Spacing enum.Spacing.html
      text Indicates whether a Punct token can join with the following token to form a multi-character operator.
      link TokenTree enum.TokenTree.html
      text A single token or a delimited sequence of token trees (e.g., [1, (), ..]).
      row
        link ConversionErrorKind enum.ConversionErrorKind.html
        text Experimental
      text Errors returned when trying to retrieve a literal unescaped value.
      row
        link EscapeError enum.EscapeError.html
        text Experimental
      text Mostly relating to malformed escape sequences, but also a few other problems.
      row
        link Level enum.Level.html
        text Experimental
      text An enum representing a diagnostic level.
    h2 Traits§
    row
      row
        link MultiSpan trait.MultiSpan.html
        text Experimental
      text Trait implemented by types that can be converted into a set of Spans.
      row
        link ToTokens trait.ToTokens.html
        text Experimental
      text Types that can be interpolated inside a  invocation.
      link quote! macro.quote.html
    h2 Functions§
    row
      link is_available fn.is_available.html
      text Determines whether proc_macro has been made accessible to the currently running program.
      row
        link quote fn.quote.html
        text Experimental
      text Quote a TokenStream into a TokenStream. This is the actual implementation of the quote!() proc macro.
      row
        link quote_span fn.quote_span.html
        text Experimental
      text Quote a Span into a TokenStream. This is needed to implement a custom quoter.
